    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. When you mention looking at crime rates and local business ownership, are there specific trends or types of demographic shifts that usually signal a higher risk of volatility? For example, does a high concentration of certain immigrant groups or a sudden change in the ethnic makeup of a district typically correlate with higher risk profiles in your modeling?",
